p08uOB-dBVP8VIh7YvjuQ_19V78eH178BAAD__55CaDc Think of Delphi as a complemen=
t to Discord and office hours: you can ask it any question about evals and =
get an instant response, whether you are debugging code, clarifying a conce=
pt, or looking for examples. The interface looks like the screenshot attach=
ed below.=C2=A0Keep in mind that Delphi is fully experimental. It may not s=
ound like us, and its answers can be vague or even incorrect. To get the mo=
st value out of Delphi, keep these guidelines in mind:Be specific. Provide =
context and details about your situation rather than asking broad questions=
=2E For example:Instead of: =E2=80=9CHow=20=
do I evaluate my legal RAG system?=
=E2=80=9DTry: =E2=80=9CI=E2=80=99m building a RAG system that retrieves cas=
e law relevant to motions under California=E2=80=99s Racial Justice Act. Th=
e model generates candidate passages for attorneys to cite in their filings=
=2E My concern is whether the retrieval=
 is surfacing precedent that is both o=
n-point and still good law. What evaluation methods should I use to measure=
 retrieval quality and detect when the system cites outdated or overturned =
cases?=E2=80=9DAsk follow-ups. If an answer feels vague or incomplete, push=
 further and ask clarifying questions. For example:Instead of stopping at: =
=E2=80=9CDelphi says: you can use precision and recall to evaluate retrieva=
l.=E2=80=9DFollow up with: =E2=80=9CCan you show me how to calculate precis=
ion and recall for my dataset of 200 Racial Justice Act motions, where each=
 motion can have multiple relevant cases? How would you define a =E2=80=98r=
elevant=E2=80=99 case in this context, and what baseline numbers should I e=
xpect?=E2=80=9DRephrase your question. Try different phrasings of the same =
question. For example:Less effective: =E2=80=9CWhen should I use pairwise c=
omparisons?=E2=80=9DMore effective: =E2=80=9CWhen should I use pairwise com=
parisons and when should I not? Can you give me a concrete example? Which a=
pproach should I start with?=E2=80=9DCross-check. Use Delphi alongside Disc=
ord discussions and office hours, not in place of them! We are looking at a=
ll our data (aka your queries), but since this is the first time we are usi=
ng Delphi, we do not know how good it will be.If you notice an incorrect or=
 unhelpful answer, let us know in Discord so we can improve it for everyone=
=2EOther StuffLifetime access and retak=
es. You will have lifetime access to a=
ll course recordings, slides, and materials, as well as to our Discord comm=
